 We have $a_{n + 2} = a_{n + 1} + a_n$. Dividing both sides by $4^{n + 3}$ and subtracting $4^{-(n + 4)}$ from both sides, we obtain:
\begin{align*}
\frac{a_{n + 2}}{4^{n + 3}} &= \frac{a_{n + 1}}{4^{n + 3}} + \frac{a_n}{4^{n + 3}} - 4^{-(n + 4)} \\
\Rightarrow \frac{a_{n + 2}}{4^{n + 3}} - \frac{a_{n + 1}}{4^{n + 2}} - \frac{a_n}{4^{n + 3}} &= -4^{-(n + 4)} \\
\Rightarrow x^{n + 2} - x^{n + 1} - x^n &= -4^{-(n + 4)}
\end{align*}
where $\frac{a_n}{4^{n + 1}} = x^n$. Now $x^3 = x^2 + x$ and $x^3/16 = x^2/4 + x/16$. Using the fact that $x^3 = x^2 + x$ repeatedly, we can eliminate $x^3$ from every equation except the first. Therefore,
\begin{align*}
x^3 &= x^2 + x = x(1 + x) = x\left(1 + \frac{x^2}{4}\right) = x + \frac{x^3}{4} = x\left(1 + \frac{x}{4}\right) \\
\Rightarrow x^3/4 &= x + \frac{x^3}{16} \\
\Rightarrow x^3/64 &= x^2/4 + \frac{x^3}{4096} \\
\Rightarrow x^3/16384 &= x/16 + \frac{x^3}{33554432}
\end{align*}
Hence, $x/16 = -4^{-5}$ and $x/4096 = -4^{-7}$. Then $a_n/4^{n + 1} = x^n = (-4)^{-n}$. Since $(-4)^{-n} = (-1)^n 4^{-n}$, \[
\sum_{n = 1}^\infty \frac{a_n}{4^{n + 1}} = \sum_{n = 1}^\infty (-1)^n 4^{-n} = \boxed{-\frac{1}{3}}.
\]
